INT. ORBITAL ALGAE FARM - MAIN BAY - CONTINUOUS

A cylindrical chamber forty meters long, lined with transparent tubes of glowing green algae that pulse with the station's slow rotation. The air smells of wet leaves and ozone. Catwalks cross overhead.

CAPTAIN YARA OKONJO (40s, grey flight suit, braided hair, a data slate strapped to her forearm) walks the central catwalk with TECH BOONE (30s, grease-stained coveralls, wild beard). DR. SELVAM (60s, white lab coat, thick spectacles) is on his knees at the base of a tube, scraping a sample from a cracked seal. ARI (teen, apprentice, oversized hood, bare feet) crouches next to him, holding a petri dish. In the control booth at the far end, PILOT KESTREL (30s, flight jacket, mirror shades pushed up on her head) leans on a console, feet on the desk. OLU (50s, station cook, apron, a ladle in his hand) stands under the first tube and peers up.

YARA
Boone, give me the pressure.

BOONE
Eleven-oh. Holding.

YARA
The seals?

BOONE
Doc says the third one's cracked.

SELVAM
(from the floor)
It's not cracked, it's weeping. There is a difference.

OLU
(from below)
There is no difference when it's my kitchen being flooded with green soup.

ARI
Doctor, the sample's turning yellow.

Selvam snatches the dish, holds it to the light, and nods.

SELVAM
Contamination. Not severe.

YARA
Define not severe.

SELVAM
We lose perhaps ten percent of the bay.

KESTREL
(over the intercom)
Captain, supply drone is two minutes out. Do I hold it?

YARA
Hold it. Boone, shut the third line.

Boone climbs down a rungs ladder, wrench in hand, moves to a manifold and cranks a valve. The glowing green in the third tube dims to dark. Ari scrambles to hold a bucket under the dripping seal. Olu walks up with his ladle and stirs the bucket thoughtfully.

OLU
This is going to be an awful dinner.

SELVAM
(dryly)
It will be a nutritious dinner.

YARA
Doctor, can the rest of the bay survive?

SELVAM
Without the third line, yes. For six days.

YARA
Then we have six days.

She taps her slate. The station hums. Overhead, the tubes pulse green in unison, and every one of them keeps living.
